---
// Set up in three steps, with what "tell your agent" looks like in each harness.
---

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="steps-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="steps-h">Set up in three steps</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">Your agent does the setup. You sign in to Cloudflare, create one token and approve each machine.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Tell your agent</h3>
          <p>It reads llms.txt, checks the prerequisites and deploys OpenBus to your own Cloudflare account, on a hostname you pick. You need a Cloudflare account with a domain on it.</p>
          <span class="step-chip mono" aria-hidden="true"><span class="caret">›</span><span>install open-bus.ai/llms.txt</span></span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Sign in to Cloudflare</h3>
          <p>Allow the Wrangler login in your browser. Then create the one API token setup asks for, from a pre-filled link. The token never goes in the chat.</p>
          <span class="step-chip" aria-hidden="true">Allow Wrangler to manage your account? <span class="mini-btn">Allow</span></span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Add your machines</h3>
          <p>Your agent runs <code>npx @open-bus/cli install</code>. Approve the machine in the browser that opens; the code is good for 10 minutes. Repeat on each machine.</p>
          <span class="step-chip" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mono">Approve leo-macbook-pro?</span> <span class="mini-btn">Approve</span></span>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="harness">
        <p class="harness-cap">The same sentence works in Claude Code, OpenCode and Pi.</p>
      <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Your agent">
        <button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" id="tab-claude" aria-controls="panel-claude" aria-selected="true"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Claude Code</button>
        <button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" id="tab-opencode" aria-controls="panel-opencode" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>OpenCode</button>
        <button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" id="tab-pi" aria-controls="panel-pi" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Pi</button>
      </div>
      <figure class="term" role="tabpanel" id="panel-claude" aria-labelledby="tab-claude">
        <div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>claude · ~/code</span></div>
<pre><span class="t-muted">&gt;</span> <span class="t-ink">install open-bus.ai/llms.txt</span>

<span class="t-accent">●</span> Fetch(<span class="t-accent">https://open-bus.ai/llms.txt</span>)
  <span class="t-muted">⎿  Set up OpenBus</span>
<span class="t-accent">●</span> Bash(node --version &amp;&amp; pnpm --version &amp;&amp; git --version)
  <span class="t-muted">⎿  v22.11.0 · 10.6.5 · 2.47.1</span>
<span class="t-accent">●</span> Bash(git clone --depth 1 --branch "$TAG" … ~/open-bus)
<span class="t-accent">●</span> Bash(cd ~/open-bus &amp;&amp; pnpm install)
<span class="t-accent">●</span> Bash(npx wrangler whoami --json)
  <span class="t-muted">⎿  Not logged in</span>
<span class="t-accent">●</span> Let's sign you in to Cloudflare. Type this, then allow
  access in the browser that opens:
  <span class="t-ink">! npx wrangler login</span></pre>
      </figure>
      <figure class="term" role="tabpanel" id="panel-opencode" aria-labelledby="tab-opencode" hidden>
        <div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>opencode · ~/code</span></div>
<pre><span class="t-accent">┃</span> <span class="t-ink">install open-bus.ai/llms.txt</span>

<span class="t-muted">⚙</span> webfetch <span class="t-accent">https://open-bus.ai/llms.txt</span>
  I'll deploy OpenBus to your Cloudflare account. Checking what you have.
<span class="t-muted">$</span> node --version; pnpm --version; git --version
<span class="t-muted">$</span> git clone --depth 1 --branch "$TAG" … ~/open-bus
<span class="t-muted">$</span> pnpm install
<span class="t-muted">$</span> npx wrangler whoami --json
  <span class="t-muted">Not logged in</span>
  Please run <span class="t-ink">npx wrangler login</span> and allow access in the browser.
  Tell me when it's done.</pre>
      </figure>
      <figure class="term" role="tabpanel" id="panel-pi" aria-labelledby="tab-pi" hidden>
        <div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>pi · ~/code</span></div>
<pre><span class="t-muted">&gt;</span> <span class="t-ink">install open-bus.ai/llms.txt</span>

<span class="t-muted">fetch</span> <span class="t-accent">https://open-bus.ai/llms.txt</span>
  I'll deploy OpenBus to your Cloudflare account.
<span class="t-muted">bash</span> node --version &amp;&amp; pnpm --version &amp;&amp; git --version
<span class="t-muted">bash</span> git clone --depth 1 --branch "$TAG" … ~/open-bus
<span class="t-muted">bash</span> pnpm install
<span class="t-muted">bash</span> npx wrangler whoami --json
  <span class="t-muted">Not logged in</span>
  You're not signed in to Cloudflare. Run <span class="t-ink">npx wrangler login</span>,
  allow access in the browser, and I'll carry on.</pre>
      </figure>
    </div>

    </div>
  </section>

<script>
  // Agent tabs (WAI-ARIA tabs: arrow keys move between them).
  const tabs = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]')];
  const select = (tab: HTMLButtonElement) => {
    for (const t of tabs) {
      const on = t === tab;
      t.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(on));
      t.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
      const panel = document.getElementById(t.getAttribute("aria-controls") ?? "");
      if (panel) panel.hidden = !on;
    }
  };
  for (const [i, tab] of tabs.entries()) {
    tab.addEventListener("click", () => select(tab));
    tab.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
      const d = e.key === "ArrowRight" ? 1 : e.key === "ArrowLeft" ? -1 : 0;
      if (!d) return;
      const next = tabs[(i + d + tabs.length) % tabs.length];
      select(next);
      next.focus();
    });
  }
</script>
